@* A feature the selected engine genuinely does not have.

   Distinct from an empty list, and the distinction is the whole point. "No volumes yet" invites
   the user to make one; this says the concept does not exist here, names the engine, and says what
   this engine does instead.

   No button of its own: the page's chrome already carries "Switch engine…", which is where a
   page's actions live and the only thing that would change the answer. Two identical buttons a
   centimetre apart read as a mistake.

   DESIGN.md section 6: never "Nothing here." Say why. *@
@inject EngineManager Engine

<EmptyState Icon="Icon" Title="@Title" Body="@Body" />

@code {
    /// <summary>The plural noun, lowercase: "volumes", "networks", "stacks".</summary>
    [Parameter, EditorRequired] public string Feature { get; set; } = "";

    [Parameter] public IconRef Icon { get; set; } = IconRef.Info;

    /// <summary>What the user can do on this engine instead, when there is something. One sentence.</summary>
    [Parameter] public string? Instead { get; set; }

    string EngineName => Engine.Selected?.Name ?? "This engine";

    string Title => $"{EngineName} has no {Feature}";

    string Body => Instead is { Length: > 0 } instead
        ? $"This is not a Docker-compatible engine, and {Feature} are not part of it. {instead}"
        : $"This is not a Docker-compatible engine, and {Feature} are not part of it. "
          + "Switching to a Docker-compatible host brings this page back.";
}
